{{!-- Which locale's hero renders at the top of a channel, and nothing else.

     The hero is `posts`[0] (partials/featured-hero*.hbs): no query, no filter, no theme
     setting. `locale` picks the wording — the three heroes are separate files because
     their label/date/reading-time strings are literals printed inside `{{#foreach}}`,
     where Ghost drops partial hash arguments.

     `/` passes `locale="en"`: the root channel is the mixed feed, and it renders inside
     default.hbs, so its hero speaks English regardless of which post is newest.
     The page guard lives in the hero partials; page 2 renders no hero at all. --}}
{{#match locale "=" "es"}}{{> "featured-hero-es"}}
{{else match locale "=" "br"}}{{> "featured-hero-br"}}
{{else}}{{> "featured-hero"}}{{/match}}
